The files in this directory are copied unchanged from matplotlib 3.11
(lib/matplotlib/backends/web_backend/ and lib/matplotlib/mpl-data/images/):

    Copyright (c) 2012- Matplotlib Development Team; All Rights Reserved

Summary of changes, as section 3 of the license below asks: none to the
files themselves. plt-rs serves them from its own HTTP server instead of
Tornado: it fills the placeholders of single_figure.html and
all_figures.html the way the Tornado templates would, and appends the
toolbar items and file formats to js/mpl.js as matplotlib's
FigureManagerWebAgg.get_javascript does.

The toolbar images in images/ are also the toolbar icons of plt-rs'
figure windows in matplotlib's look (crates/plt/src/gui/images.rs, which
embeds these same files), drawn as matplotlib's Tk toolbar draws them:
the 24-pixel image on 1x screens and the _large one on 2x screens, faded
while their button is disabled. Only the windows use the subplots,
qt4_editor_options and help images.

The ResizeObserver polyfill at the end of js/mpl.js is JSXTools' resize
observer, dedicated to the public domain under CC0-1.0.

matplotlib's license follows.

